From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:56:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Enable the eMMC

The Cubie A7S can carry an 8-bit eMMC on SMHC2, but the board file
leaves the controller off, so the eMMC is not seen.

Enable SMHC2 with an 8-bit bus, as non-removable, with its hardware reset
line (PC1) and HS200 at 1.8 V. VCC comes from the 3.3 V supply that also
feeds the SD slot (vcc-3v3), VCCQ from the PMIC's 1.8 V CLDO5 output,
which is described as a fixed regulator that the boot firmware leaves on
until the AXP318W has a driver. Add an mmc2 alias, so the eMMC keeps its
index next to the SD card. Boards sold without eMMC get a controller that
finds no card.

Not covered: HS400, the PMIC rails, and vcc-pc-supply for the pin bank,
whose bias setting the A733 pin controller driver does not model yet.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; on the board with an eMMC
it appears with its boot partitions, and reading 256 MiB gives no data
error; on the board without one the controller finds no card.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts   | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index db942dc0123f..55e1dabb6c1f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ / {
 	aliases {
 		serial0 = &uart0;
 		mmc0 = &mmc0;
+		mmc2 = &mmc2;
 	};
 
 	chosen {
@@ -56,6 +57,15 @@ scp@48100000 {
 		};
 	};
 
+	/* CLDO5 of the PMIC: VCC-PC and with it the eMMC VCCQ */
+	reg_vcc1v8: vcc1v8 {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "vcc-1v8";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+	};
+
 	reg_vcc3v3: vcc3v3 {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "vcc-3v3";
@@ -73,6 +83,16 @@ &mmc0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&mmc2 {
+	vmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
+	vqmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc1v8>;
+	bus-width = <8>;
+	non-removable;
+	cap-mmc-hw-reset;
+	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &osc {
 	clock-frequency = <26000000>;
 };
